# Flow review process artifacts.
#
# Repository precedent for merged feature PRs is to carry NO .flow/reviews
# files at all — only the terminal verdict, the durable baseline receipt, and
# a consolidated landing record are worth version control. Everything below is
# an orchestration transcript, session telemetry, or a regenerable tool
# output: not a governance record, and it bloats feature PRs.
.flow/reviews/*.events.jsonl
.flow/reviews/*.log
.flow/reviews/**/*.log
.flow/reviews/*.raw.txt
.flow/reviews/*.raw.json
.flow/reviews/*-prompt.md
.flow/reviews/*.prompt.md
.flow/reviews/*.schema.json
# Harness *result* envelopes: model, session id, token counts, USD cost. Scoped
# to the `.result.json` suffix the harness itself emits — deliberately NOT
# `*.receipt.json`, which would also swallow governance receipts such as
# .flow/reviews/fn-112-baseline-receipt.json.
.flow/reviews/*.result.json
# Local convenience symlink into a session-scoped debug log.
.flow/reviews/latest
# Regenerable browser-evidence and live-QA output directories. The smoke script
# (scripts/pdf-viewer-smoke.ts) writes the first; both are reproducible, and
# their measurements are summarized in the landing record.
.flow/reviews/fn-112-task-6-evidence/
.flow/reviews/fn-112-qa-evidence/

